    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μικτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mixed, blended</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				22d
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁπλοῦς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				547e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐκ τούτων</span>
			<i>compounded</i> of these, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				837b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				41
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					1.2.27
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.703
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>motley,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1153.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. (In early texts <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεικτός</span></b>  (which is written in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				292.25
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>) shd. prob. be restored, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείγνυμι.</span>
			)</div>
